# Component BEM Styling

BEM class names; blocks are reusable base classes, not unique-per-component.

```
.block / .block__element / .block--modifier / .block__element--modifier
```

- Reuse generic blocks (`.card`, not `.asset-card`). React provides identity; CSS provides the visual pattern. Prefer modifiers (`.card--compact`) over new blocks.
- kebab-case only; no `block__element__sub`.
- Each component owns its `styles.css` with additions only when reusing a base block. Import the base stylesheet if there are no additions.
- Group selectors: block → elements → modifiers.
